      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785274278769,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Assuming we've already check that the valeus are all positive, the intensity of a colour can be given by\nthe difference between the three coordinates.\n\nIn the center point, where the intensity is in its lowest, alpha = beta = gamma = 1/3",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Assuming we've already check that the valeus are all positive, the intensity of a colour can be given by\nthe difference between the three coordinates.\n\nIn the center point, where the intensity is in its lowest, alpha = beta = gamma = 1/3",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
